title Caravan cycle -- a ring is the shape with no ends, and no domain inside it sees the whole
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, condense REMEMBER, send the finished increment.
think Standfast first. The living REDS rows (80, 83, 84, 85) and every prose note read closed and released; the one I could not confirm by reading alone was 84, whose root was a missing gitignore allowlist, so I checked the file rather than the note -- both `!/work-in-progress/` and `!/crux/` stand at lines 68 and 69. No open agent-closable red, so the constructive queue opens.
think The running thread came from the last three logs, whose recommends agree on one next rung: the cycle. relay.rye closed the chain by seating a domain that both asks and answers, and named the open question -- two relays wired to each other, a flow graph that closes on itself, and whether a closed graph with no waiting verb still settles.
think Council rota, lap 459 of the 27-doc d27 -- item 27, recursion-prompts/README.md. Its balance compass is what this round was ordered by: TAME governs the code, reds-first governs the corrective queue, Lindy-first crux-first orders the constructive one, and a witness on metal closes a claim rather than a sentence. Its closing line also names the standard this rung had to meet -- every stop inside the route green, every gate outside it named.
think The shape question came first, and it changed the design. A pair of mutual relays would have given a cycle of length two, which is what every ask-and-answer declaration in this arc already carries: relay's own ask_up and answer_up are a two-cycle in flow terms. So the honest ring is three domains circulating one direction -- alder to birch to cedar and home -- where the closure is a fact about the whole rather than about a pair.
think Two derivations fall out of the grants and neither needs a role word. In a chain, two domains span exactly one peer and those are its ends; in a ring every domain spans exactly two, so a ring is the shape with no ends. And exactly one directed walk visits every domain once and returns where it began, found by a bounded backtracking search over the flow graph, which yields the circulation order.
think The deadlock question answered itself structurally, and the answer is sharper than I expected. A ring is the textbook circular-wait shape, yet circular wait is a property of waiting rather than of circles -- no verb here waits, so a badly ordered pass costs a pass and never the ring. The run proves it: alder reading for its lap before cedar has rung hears Unheard and returns, and the lap still closes on the passes that follow.
think The finding worth carrying is what the ring takes away. In the chain, the relay held a grant on every region and could total the whole run from inside it; around a ring no domain can. alder reads three regions of four and the arc between the other two is refused NotGranted. A ring has no vantage point -- only the parent outside it sees the whole, which is what a supervisor is for.
think One more fact turns on the closure, and it inverts the fanin law by exactly one lap. At one hop, the region an ask arrives in names its author and the bytes name its origin, and the two agree. After a full circuit they must disagree: bytes reaching alder from cedar, naming alder, are alder's own ask come home. The disagreement is the signature of a completed lap, and a homecoming refuses any ask still naming a stranger.
obs Reuse over restatement -- flows_of, peer_span, HopList, ask_text and asked_origin all came from relay.rye by import rather than by copy, so the ring adds arithmetic (has_flow, ring_order, reach_of, widest_reach) and nothing already proven.
obs The vantage check is honestly weaker than it looks, and the README says so. Under one-writer-one-reader flows, a domain reaching every region would have to touch every other domain, which makes a star, and a star has ends -- so the vantage fact follows from the ends fact. The check stands as a guard that costs nothing rather than as an independent proof.
loom witness=caravan_cycle_witness asks=4 domains=3 flows=4 grants=8 laps=1 arcs=8 bells=6 rings=3 reach=3of4
loom red_probe=reversed_edge result=walk_closed_nowhere outcome=the_grants_close_on_no_single_lap
loom red_probe=chain_declaration result=two_domains_span_other_than_two outcome=the_shape_has_an_end
file caravan/systems/serial_cycle.bron the ring declaration -- three domains, three circulating regions, one tail, and no ends anywhere in it
file caravan/cycle.rye the ring itself -- the shape derived twice from the grants, a lap that closes without waiting, an ask that comes home, and a whole no domain inside can read
file tools/caravan_cycle_witness.rish the witness, GREEN on metal, both RED paths proven before the green was trusted
file caravan/README.md the ladder row and the durable prose -- why a ring has no vantage point
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moves to the ring, the prior edges condensed to one pointer
recommend keep-going -- next the ring under fall: one domain of the circuit falls mid-lap and restarts, taking its rights from the declaration rather than from a parent's memory, while asks stand in the arcs on either side of it. rederive.rye already proves the rights come back; the open crux is what a lap owes a domain that was absent for part of it, and whether a circuit with a hole in it settles or simply waits for the hole to close. No key, no funds, no gate.
